5.During Ubuntu OS installation, you face a Kernel Panic Error. How would you troubleshoot it?
Ans:- 1. Use a Live Environment to Diagnose the Issue
•	Boot from the Ubuntu Installation USB: Instead of continuing with the installation, choose the "Try Ubuntu without installing" option to enter the live environment. 
2. Check for File System Errors 
•	Identify Your Ubuntu Partition: Use sudo fdisk -l to list your disks and partitions. Identify the device name for your Ubuntu partition (
•	Run fsck: Execute the command sudo fsck -f /dev/sdXX  which will check and repair the filesystem. 
3. Consider Hardware and Configuration Issues
•	BIOS/UEFI Settings:
•	Disable Secure Boot: This can sometimes interfere with Linux installations.
•	Check Disk Mode
•	Corrupted Installation Media:
•	Download a new ISO: Get a fresh copy of the Ubuntu ISO file.
•	Rewrite the USB: Use a different utility to write the ISO to the USB drive. 
4. Generate a New Initial RAM Disk (initramfs) 
•	Update the initramfs: Run sudo update-initramfs -u -k all in the terminal of the live environment or within the chroot session to regenerate the initial RAM disk for all installed kernels. 


